{
  "title": "First declension: feminine nouns",
  "note": "First-declension nouns are mostly feminine. Nouns in -η keep η in the singular: ἀρχή, ἀρχῆς, ἀρχῇ, ἀρχήν. After ε, ι or ρ the vowel is α: ἡμέρα, ἡμέρας, ἡμέρᾳ, ἡμέραν. Nouns in short -α after other letters switch to η in the genitive and dative: δόξα, δόξης, δόξῃ, δόξαν. All share one plural: -αι, -ῶν, -αις, -ας.",
